  8	Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.
  9	
 10	## Validation at execute time
 11	
 12	- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16); [validated by: returns a required-property rejection without invoking the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L6)).
 13	- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46)).
 14	- When valid input includes undeclared extra properties, `ToolRegistry.execute` passes the input through unchanged and invokes the executor exactly once ([validated by: passes valid input with extra properties through unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L32)).
 15	- For a nested wrong-typed value, the rejection names its full property path and expected type without echoing the value ([validated by: names the full nested property path when a value has the wrong type](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L50)).
 16	- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults.
 17	- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake.
 18	
 19	## Schema compilation and caching
 20	
 21	- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
 22	- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: static schemas compile once across repeated executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L30)).
 23	- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules.
 24	
 25	## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery
 26	
 27	- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
 28	- `processMessage` resolves after the provider receives a rejected tool call as a result and retries with corrected arguments ([validated by: returns an input rejection to the provider so it can retry with corrected arguments](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L385)).

